 "header": "Insignia 55\" Class F30 4K Fire TV (NS-55F301NA25, model AFTDCT31, codename duckie), Fire OS 7 / Android 9 (SDK 28),\nfirmware PS7715.5585N. Also a good starting point for other Insignia / Toshiba / Pioneer Fire TV Edition sets on Fire OS 7.\n\nFIRE OS: DEBLOAT ONLY. Fire OS will not let a third-party launcher take over Home: com.amazon.tv.launcher and\ncom.amazon.firehomestarter are protected packages (pm disable-user is refused), their HOME filter has priority 950,\nand `cmd package set-home-activity` prints Success but is ignored. launcher/build-and-install.sh does not apply\nhere; this list removes Amazon's ads, telemetry and preloads around the stock home screen.\nLive TV app: com.amazon.tv.livetv.\n\nApply (bash):       TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/insignia-ns55f301na25/debloat.txt\nUndo  (bash):       TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/insignia-ns55f301na25/debloat.txt com.amazon.tv.launcher\nApply (PowerShell): powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools\\disable.ps1 -TvHost <tv ip> examples\\insignia-ns55f301na25\\debloat.txt\nUndo  (PowerShell): powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools\\restore.ps1 -TvHost <tv ip> examples\\insignia-ns55f301na25\\debloat.txt -StockLauncher com.amazon.tv.launcher\n(restore.sh re-enables the stock launcher as a matter of routine; on Fire OS it was never disabled, which is harmless.)\nEverything is DISABLED for user 0, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nKeep enabled: com.amazon.tv.livetv, com.amazon.tv.quicksettings and com.amazon.tv.settings.v2 (HDMI/tuner inputs and\nthe Picture/Sound/System settings), com.apple.airplay.amazon.airplay if you use AirPlay/HomeKit.\nTwo packages in the telemetry group, com.amazon.device.metrics and com.amazon.ftvads.deeplinking, were reported as\nprotected on a Toshiba Fire TV (Fire OS 7): if disable.sh prints an error for them, that is why; everything else applies.\nThe Alexa, Prime Video, cast and OTA groups below are personal choices, marked as such: comment out what you use.",
